<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tibet–Ladakh–Mughal War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1679">1679</a>–<a href="/years/1684">1684</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>–Ladakh–Mughal War was fought from 1679 to 1684 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganden-monastery">Ganden</a> Phodrang government of Tibet under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/5th-dalai-lama">Fifth Dalai Lama</a> and the kingdom of Ladakh. A Tibetan and Mongol army invaded Ladakh and besieged Basgo, and Ladakh obtained help from the Mughal governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tingmosgang">Treaty of Tingmosgang</a> of 1684 fixed the border and left western Tibet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a>.</p></div>
